# Poriscope code owners
#
# ADVISORY ONLY. This file exists so that a pull request automatically requests review
# from whoever knows the code it touches. It is NOT a merge gate: "Require review from
# Code Owners" is deliberately switched off in branch protection, and nothing here
# blocks a contribution. If you are contributing a plugin from a fork, you do not need
# an owner's approval to merge.
#
# Ownership here reflects who maintains a file today, which is not always the same as
# the "# Contributors:" header at the top of it -- headers record authorship, including
# that of people no longer with the lab, whose files have passed to @shadowk29.
#
# Patterns are last-match-wins, so the order below matters: the global fallback first,
# then broad rules, then the file-level carve-outs.
#
# GitHub only auto-requests users with write access to the repository; a line naming
# anyone else is silently ignored.
#
# See docs/source/utils/user_manuals/plugins_manual/development_workflow/code_ownership.rst

